	help
	  driver/drivers/mipi_dsi/dsi_yakogl_samsung.c, a Zephyr MIPI-DSI
	  device whose register logic is driver/rust/src/ip/samsung_dsim.rs and
	  ip/dphy_timing.rs (from IMX8MPRM Rev. 3 13.6 / 13.7 and the MIPI
	  D-PHY v1.2 minimums), in place of src/display/imx8mp_dsim.c: the
	  chain facade attaches the display node's `dsi` through it
	  (src/display/imx8mp_dsim_rust.c). Off until it has run on the
	  Verdin (driver/docs/imx8mp-display-cold.md). Outside the
	  SAFEUI_DISPLAY_IMX8MP block: selecting MIPI_DSI under its I2C
	  dependency makes a Kconfig loop.

